module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_unreached_effect_leg_reads_as_one_that_ran_and_refused

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data an_unreached_effect_leg_reads_as_one_that_ran_and_refused: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_unreached_effect_leg_reads_as_one_that_ran_and_refused" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an unreached effect leg reads as one that ran and refused** (a remote effect whose transport never reached the host -- ssh could not connect, so no remote shell began -- is reported with the same value as a leg whose script ran and refused, so the caller can neither retry the first without retrying the second nor resume the leftovers the first one strands).",

    "INVALID STATE: gunbc.spark.pair_serving_apply SparkPairHostApplyOutcome had two arms, Applied and Failed, and every non-zero session result became Failed. ssh(1)'s own 255 (extdeps.ssh.session ssh_client_error_exit_status) was folded into the script's refusal exits.",

    "HARM: fleet-converge run 36918167575 (2026-10-01, mode spark_v41_group_a_launch). One leg to srv7 timed out over Wi-Fi (`ssh: connect to host 192.168.1.232 port 22: Connection timed out`), the whole four-host transaction rolled back, the rollback leg to srv7 timed out too, and srv7 kept `.gunbc-had-no-unit` and `.gunbc-transaction`. Every later run refused at preflight until a human deleted them. A transient link loss cost a full arm abort plus a manual intervention.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: whether a remote shell reported BEGINNING. gunbc.spark.pair_serving_apply spark_pair_leg_payload wraps every privileged script to print a began-line before its first effect and its own exit after its last; spark_pair_leg_outcome_of reads Unreached only when neither line arrived AND ssh exited 255. A began-line with no exit line is a script that RAN to an unknown point and is Failed, never retried. stderr text is not the discriminator (gunbc.command_runner ssh_exit_255_conflation_dissolution rejects stderr-sniffing).",

    "RESIDUE, STATED: a connection lost after the shell started but before its began-line crossed also reads Unreached. gunbc.spark.native_serving_apply therefore retries only idempotent stages: observe, preflight and the front door read, the stop reaches the same stopped rank however often it is sent, the commit rewrites the same committed-arm record, and apply's unconditional restart is the module's declared epoch semantics. (Until 2026-10-05 the stages were preserve/commit/rollback with per-transaction no-op checks; the arm converge, docs/plans/arm-convergence-recovery-design.md, retired them.)",

    "RUNG: found at 1 (mitigatable -- a human could read the log and delete the files). Now 2 for the native serving arm: witnesses in dag/test/claim/spark/native_serving_resumable_apply_witness_test.dag pin the reading and the bounded retry (spark_native_unreached_leg_attempt_budget) with discriminating reds. The leftover decision they also pinned was retired with the leftover classifier (docs/plans/arm-convergence-recovery-design.md): an unreached leg's host is now read by the next converge's observation as an unread rank, which refuses rather than being classified. CEILING 3: an outcome type every remote-effect leg must produce, so no consumer can match a leg result without facing the Unreached arm. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the other SshSessionExecResult consumers that fold 255 into a refusal (gunbc.spark.model_snapshot_materialize spark_remote_run, gunbc.host_command_binding host_command_outcome_of's Unconfirmed arm) consuming one shared in-band leg reading, SUFFICIENT FOR no remote-effect consumer in the corpus to construct a ran-and-refused value from a leg that never began. PROGRESS (2026-10-04): gunbc.spark.model_snapshot_materialize spark_remote_run now consumes the ONE shared in-band reading, gunbc.spark.remote_leg_began (lifted out of gunbc.spark.pair_serving_apply, which consumes it too; review of gunbc#13204), and returns RemoteUnreachable with reach LegBeginUnobserved for ssh's 255 with no began-line received, projected to ArgvLegMayHaveRun, never ArgvLegDidNotRun: the marker and the command share one unacknowledged stream, so a missing marker does not establish that nothing ran (see a_dark_management_lan_leg_hangs_and_reads_as_a_down_host). The same residue applies to this row's own Unreached reading. gunbc.host_command_binding host_command_outcome_of remains.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
